.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "configure add client name=fd2 address=fd2.example.org password=secret"
add a client
.TP
.B "configure add console name=ops password=pw profile=operator"
a console with the rights of a profile
.TP
.B "configure update schedule=Nightly run=\(dqFull sun at 23:00\(dq run=\(dqIncremental mon\-sat at 23:00\(dq"
replace the Run lines (Onesimus)
.TP
.B "configure export client=bareos\-fd"
write the director resource for the file daemon of bareos\-fd
.TP
.B "configure delete schedule=OldNightly"
remove an unused schedule (Onesimus)
.TP
.B "configure add pool name=Weekly pooltype=Backup maximumvolumejobs=1 labelformat=Weekly\-"
a new backup pool with one job per volume
.TP
.B "configure add schedule name=Nightly run=\(dqFull 1st sun at 23:05\(dq run=\(dqIncremental mon\-sat at 23:05\(dq"
a schedule with two run lines
.TP
.B "configure add job name=BackupClient2 jobdefs=DefaultJob client=bareos\-fd"
a job whose required directives come from a jobdefs
.TP
.B "configure export client=bareos\-fd"
export the director resource for bareos\-fd
.TP
.B "configure read client=bareos\-fd"
summary of a client
.TP
.B "configure read job=BackupClient1"
summary of a job
.TP
.B "configure update client=bareos\-fd address=fd.example.org port=9112"
change the address and port of a client
.TP
.B "configure update job=BackupClient1 description="
remove the description of a job
.TP
.B "configure delete fileset=OldFileSet"
delete a fileset no job uses any more
.TP
.B "configure delete client=old\-fd"
delete a client, refused while a job still names it
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command. Onesimus extensions: configure add console, configure read, configure update, configure delete.
